    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Crucial distinction: SPSC members are appointed by the Governor, but their removal power lies exclusively with the President of India.",
        "The retirement age for SPSC members was increased from 60 to 62 years by the 41st Constitutional Amendment Act, 1976.",
        "Unlike UPSC and SPSC, a Joint State Public Service Commission (JSPSC) is a statutory body created by an Act of Parliament, not a constitutional body."
      ],
      "id": "hpqzzjz"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Both UPSC and State Public Service Commissions (SPSC) are constitutional bodies provided under Articles 315 to 323 in Part XIV of the Indian Constitution.",
        "The Chairman and members of UPSC are appointed and removed by the President of India.",
        "The Chairman and members of SPSC are appointed by the Governor of the state, but can be removed only by the President of India.",
        "The retirement age for UPSC members is 65 years, whereas for SPSC members it is 62 years.",
        "UPSC submits its annual report to the President, while SPSC submits its annual report to the Governor of the state."
      ],
      "id": "0ovsi2o"
    }
